  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner from Melton, Leicestershire, who was paralysed in a 2007 riding accident, has died following an accident in Jordan on 22 August. She raised nearly £1m through high-profile challenges, including completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days in a bionic suit and lighting the Paralympic cauldron that year. In 2016, while pregnant, she completed the Great North Run in five days. Her family said they are devastated and requested privacy.",
